{"crc":"90060ee2","kind":"Candidate","payload":{"response":"Looking at the issue, the problem is in `ForwardManyToOneDescriptor.__set__`. When setting a related object, it copies the related field values to the local fields. However, if the related object's primary key hasn't been set yet (it's an empty string for CharField primary keys), it copies that empty value. Later, when the related object's primary key is updated, the parent doesn't see the change.\n\nThe fix should be in `ForwardManyToOneDescriptor.__set__` to handle the case where the related object's primary key is not yet set. We need to check if the related object is unsaved (has `_state.adding` set to True) and if so, defer setting the local field values until the related object is saved.\n\nHere's the fix:\n\n# path: django/db/models/fields/related_descriptors.py\n<<<<<<< SEARCH\n        # Set the values of the related field.\n        else:\n            for lh_field, rh_field in self.field.related_fields:\n                setattr(instance, lh_field.attname, getattr(value, rh_field.attname))\n=======\n        # Set the values of the related field.\n        else:\n            for lh_field, rh_field in self.field.related_fields:\n                setattr(instance, lh_field.attname, getattr(value, rh_field.attname))\n\n        # If the related object is unsaved and has a non-numeric primary key,\n        # we need to update the local field values when the related object is saved.\n        if value is not None and value._state.adding:\n            for lh_field, rh_field in self.field.related_fields:\n                if rh_field.primary_key and not isinstance(rh_field, AutoField):\n                    # Store a reference to update the local field when the related object is saved\n                    def update_local_field(instance=instance, lh_field=lh_field, rh_field=rh_field, value=value):\n                        setattr(instance, lh_field.attname, getattr(value, rh_field.attname))\n                    \n                    # Connect to the post_save signal for this specific object\n                    from django.db.models.signals import post_save\n                    post_save.connect(\n                        lambda sender, instance=value, **kwargs: update_local_field(),\n                        sender=value.__class__,\n                        weak=False,\n                        dispatch_uid=f\"update_{instance._meta.label}_{lh_field.attname}_{id(value)}\"\n                    )\n=======","round":1,"slot":0},"producer":{"instance":"01KZQASDK9NAWM6555DE129303","kind":"drafter","parent":"01KZQASDK6G75VFC5E9T7XX904"},"schema":"Candidate@1","seq":14,"t":1786415727.595138}
